# Models are fetched at runtime and verified against shipped checksums, never vendored.
# 4.7 GB here is the full development manifest, not a user download: a default
# install fetches 642 MiB (Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 plus Silero VAD). The Qwen3
# GGUFs are benchmark-only, since the shipped app has no local LLM.
# Their licences differ from this repo's.
# Ignore the contents, not the directory: git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so a bare "models/" here silently kills the
# negation below.
models/*

# models.lock.json IS tracked, but it is only a record of what this checkout
# downloaded. The checksums that are enforced ship inside the app, in
# m0/lib/models.pins.json: every model file is checked against its pin before it
# is used and a mismatch is refused, so a changed or substituted download is
# caught rather than trusted.
!models/models.lock.json

node_modules/
dist/
out/

# Generated test audio: rebuildable, and large.
fixtures/*.wav

# Real meetings used for the counterfactual gate. These are private by
# definition: they are transcripts of actual conversations.
fixtures/meetings/

# Benchmark output is kept as evidence, but only the four runs named below.
# Every other run lands here unignored otherwise, and a benchmark result records
# the machine it ran on: CPU model, GPU, RAM. A contributor running `npm run m0`
# would commit their own hardware without noticing. The counterfactual summaries
# are worse again, since they carry the titles of real meetings.
# Ignore the contents, not the directory, for the same reason models/* does: a
# bare "results/" kills the negations below.
results/*
!results/asr-chunk-limit-2026-09-02T23-40-43-316Z.json
!results/bench-asr-2026-09-02T23-21-57-287Z.json
!results/bench-llm-2026-09-03T00-06-40-037Z.json
!results/bench-llm-2026-09-03T00-17-39-109Z.json

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.local

# .claude/launch.json IS tracked, so this directory is a committed one and the
# per-machine file Claude Code writes beside it lands straight in a commit.
# Named file rather than the whole directory, for the same reason models/ spells
# its exception out: excluding .claude/ would silently swallow the next config
# meant to be shared.
.claude/settings.local.json
